    "result_text": "The build is green. The full `mvnw test` run passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that creating an owner with a normalized telephone already used by another owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges (following the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` pattern):\n\n1. **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending normalized telephone.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a handler mapping `DuplicateTelephoneException` \u2192 `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409), with an `errors: [\"telephone\"]` property in the ProblemDetail body, consistent with the other owner-field handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the submitted telephone, it now calls `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)` before saving. That helper streams over `findAllOwners()`, normalizes each existing telephone the same way (strip non-digits), and throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` if any match is found.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (duplicate \u2192 409) and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (distinct numbers still succeed).",
